        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Tekton and Icon are closer in quality than their fans admit. Both make 6-point sockets, sensible combination wrenches and 90-tooth ratchets that will serve a home or independent mechanic for years, and both stand behind them for life.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy Tekton if you build your kit online, want consistent mechanisms and the easiest warranty claim going. Buy Icon if a Harbor Freight is close, you want a specialty ratchet shape, or you are happy to wait for a coupon on a full set. Mixing the two is perfectly fine.
          </p>
